slash it dash waves,

121
00:05:19,924 --> 00:05:21,610
slash dev ops dash A I.

122
00:05:21,610 --> 00:05:23,295
Install it like before,

123
00:05:23,295 --> 00:05:24,468
then run lab up,

124
00:05:24,468 --> 00:05:27,986
and work inside slash opt slash lab seventy-two.

125
00:05:28,536 --> 00:05:30,963
One: with the default memory storage,

126
00:05:30,963 --> 00:05:32,407
start the second copy,

127
00:05:32,407 --> 00:05:35,491
add item one to the cart on port five thousand,

128
00:05:35,491 --> 00:05:39,821
and save the cart of port five thousand and one in split dot text.

129
00:05:40,371 --> 00:05:43,272
Two: restart both with storage set to D B,

130
00:05:43,272 --> 00:05:44,170
add item two,

131
00:05:44,170 --> 00:05:48,798
and save the cart of port five thousand and one in shared dot text.

132
00:05:49,348 --> 00:05:51,361
Three: restart with storage D B,

133
00:05:51,361 --> 00:05:55,513
and make sure the cart on port five thousand still holds item two.

134
00:05:56,063 --> 00:06:02,006
Four: write the answer to this question in answers dot text: where does the cart live now?

135
00:06:02,006 --> 00:06:03,128
Like this: state,

136
00:06:03,128 --> 00:06:03,525
colon,

137
00:06:03,525 --> 00:06:04,383
shop dot D B.

138
00:06:04,933 --> 00:06:09,669
Five: leave the second copy running, so both servers answer with the same cart.

139
00:06:10,219 --> 00:06:12,758
Then run lab check. Five pass lines.

140
00:06:14,808 --> 00:06:16,792
Six points, and you need all six.

141
00:06:17,342 --> 00:06:19,219
The checker shows five pass lines.

142
00:06:19,769 --> 00:06:22,265
You can explain state, and give an example.

143
00:06:22,815 --> 00:06:25,183
You can explain stateful against stateless.

144
00:06:25,733 --> 00:06:28,912
You can explain why scaling out needs stateless servers.

145
00:06:29,462 --> 00:06:32,790
You can explain persistent data, and why it needs a backup.

146
